6.1 Pricing engine (critical)
For every Home Services booking:
•	worker_price is set by the partner (for example ₹100).
•	display_price = worker_price + 7% of worker_price + ₹100 (example: 100 + 7 + 100 = ₹207). The 7% and the ₹100 are two separate, configurable values in admin settings.
•	A discount is generated once, server-side, when the booking is created, as a random whole number between ₹20 and ₹50 inclusive, then stored and never regenerated (example: ₹30).
•	payable = display_price − discount (example: 207 − 30 = ₹177).
•	What the customer sees: "Service price ₹207", "Offer discount −₹30", "You pay ₹177". Label the discount "Special offer" or "Offer discount". Never use the word random.
•	Never show the customer the worker price, the 7%, the ₹100, or how the money is split. Do not mention commission anywhere in the customer UI.
•	Internal accounting (admin and ledger only): the worker payout is worker_price (₹100). SERVA's revenue is payable − worker_price (₹77, which is the 7% plus the remaining amount after the discount). Store all components on the booking record and show them in the admin settlement view. The partner sees only their own payout.
•	Apply this engine to the worker or service charge in all Home Services. For cooking, ingredient costs are passed through to the chef (see 6.4) and are not marked up. Make this configurable.
