Booking state machine
From	To	Triggered by	Rule
Request submitted	Provider assigned	Partner accepts	Partner is verified and available
Request submitted	Request submitted (re-offered)	Partner rejects or times out	Offer goes to the next eligible partner
Provider assigned	Quotation pending approval	Partner submits a quotation	Events, Agriculture, Moving, Contractors
Quotation pending approval	Confirmed	Customer approves	Events: only after the advance succeeds and the vendor accepts
Confirmed	On the way	Partner	None
On the way	Arrived	Partner	None
Arrived	In progress	Partner	None
In progress	Work completed	Partner uploads completion photos	None
Work completed	Completed	Customer confirms	Auto-confirm after 48 hours with no dispute (configurable)
Completed	Paid	Final payment succeeds	Milestone balances for Events
Any state before Completed	Cancelled	Customer or partner	Refund terms shown before payment
Any state	Issue raised	Customer	Support reviews messages and photos
Home Services have a fixed price, so payment is taken online at booking and the quotation step is skipped. Moving adds Packing in progress, Loading in progress, Vehicle departed (confirmed by the customer), Unloading and Placement. Agriculture adds Work started and Work in progress. Cooking releases the ingredient amount to the chef when the chef accepts, and holds the rest until completion (assumption, configurable).
Acceptance tests
1.	Pricing example. Worker price ₹100 gives a displayed price of ₹207. The discount is a whole number from 20 to 50, so a discount of ₹30 gives ₹177 payable. The admin ledger shows worker payout ₹100 and platform revenue of payable minus 100.
2.	Rounding. Worker price ₹250 gives 7% = 17.50, rounded half up to ₹18, so the displayed price is ₹368.
3.	Discount stability. Refreshing, retrying payment or reopening the booking never changes the discount. Across 200 simulated bookings every discount is between 20 and 50, and both limits occur.
4.	Customer privacy. In the pages, API responses and receipts, the customer never sees the worker price, the 7%, the ₹100 or the word commission.
5.	Cooking and painting payment. Only online methods are offered, and the API rejects cash with a 400 error. Cooking estimate = price per plate × people + cook service charge (₹40 × 10 + ₹500 = ₹900).
6.	Events advance. With the advance unpaid, the booking stays at Awaiting advance with no booking ID. After payment succeeds and the vendor accepts, it becomes Confirmed with a booking ID and receipt.
7.	Events quotation. The multi-service total equals the sum of the service lines, each shown separately. The sample marriage total of ₹2,90,000 gives a 30% advance of ₹87,000 and a balance of ₹2,03,000.
8.	DJ. DJ opens its own booking page directly, with no subcategory navigation. Profiles show experience, videos, availability and the total quoted price.
9.	Moving rules. Exactly seven service cards are shown, and Loading and Unloading is one card. No vehicle can be booked anywhere. The three vehicle choices are present. The API rejects a quotation line of type vehicle.
10.	Packing boxes. Five size rows (Small, Medium, Large, Extra Large, Custom) each have a quantity input that accepts zero. Sizes show inches and centimetres. Material cost is a separate quotation line.
11.	Agriculture. Three entry options are shown. Service-specific fields appear only for the chosen service (drone spraying asks for spray material and not cattle count). Area accepts acres, guntas and hectares, with 1 acre = 40 guntas and 1 hectare ≈ 2.47 acres.
12.	Home Construction. There is no payment step. The enquiry appears in the contractor dashboard with the customer's details.
13.	Partner verification. An unverified partner cannot accept a request (403). After admin approval, they can.
14.	Price labels. An initial price reads Estimated. After the partner confirms, it reads Confirmed.
15.	Revised quotes. Changing items, floors, workers or area creates a revised quotation that the customer must approve, and work cannot start before.
16.	Responsive. At 360, 768 and 1440 pixels, no page scrolls sideways.
17.	Accessibility. One booking per category can be completed with the keyboard only, and an automated audit finds no serious or critical issues.
18.	Auth. OTP success works, a wrong OTP shows an error, resend works, and attempts are rate limited after five tries.
19.	Access control. A customer cannot open partner or admin routes or APIs (403). A partner cannot read another partner's earnings.
20.	Server-side pricing. Editing the price in the browser request has no effect, and the server returns its own calculation.
21.	Language. The Telugu switch translates the navigation and home page and persists after a reload.
22.	Seed and discovery. All five categories show at least six listings with images, and search finds "electrician", "DJ" and "tractor".
